# Local activate

- “Active” means: Icerde starts the **generated** backend on localhost (Docker Compose or `go run` / stack equivalent) so Maestro and the emulator can reach it.
- Not a public URL. Not Icerde cloud.
- Track pid, port, logs, and stop on project close or user stop.
- Do not start the generated API inside the platform Go process.
- Collision: bind uncommon ports; never steal 3000/5173/8080 from the Icerde desktop UI if those are in use — pick an isolated range for generated apps.
- Read [docs/local-activate.md](docs/local-activate.md).
